WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.600
What's the point of life?

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.160
We tend to ask it as if life were

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.280
an arrow...

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.760
aimed by someone, at a target we're meant to

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:09.320
find.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.360
But as far as we can tell, nothing out

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.600
there is aiming.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.680
And yet, everything alive reaches.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.040
Toward light.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.240
Toward water.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:20.840
Toward each other.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:25.080
English has a word for that, with two meanings.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.520
To tend:

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.560
to lean toward.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.480
And to tend:

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.520
to take care of.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.280
Both grow from one Latin root, /ˈtɛndɛrɛ/...

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.080
to stretch.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.800
So here's my answer.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.480
The point of life is to tend.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.760
To stretch toward what's worth caring for:

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.840
a person, a craft, a question, a place...

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.200
and look after it.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.520
The meaning isn't waiting at the end.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.840
It's in the reaching.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:54.720
So...

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.029
what will you tend?
